      "description": "The meme uses the image of a child standing between two large costumed characters to imply that the child is 'classic' or 'authentic' in a way that is not appropriate or respectful. This relies on the real-world stereotype that children are inherently 'classic' or 'authentic' versions of things, which can be seen as infantilizing or objectifying the child. The meme does not contain any explicit abusive, cyberbullying, or hateful content, but it does contain harmful content that could be interpreted as objectifying or infantilizing the child.",
